      "title": "Identifying Parallel Vectors From a Diagram"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "00d2330f-10ff-5cb1-99e4-7884be1e423b",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186096700/plots/81231df4386e63144b950ae5232adea313ba0eea673e364f898b7aa2eeb63d91.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $b =-e$\n2. $c =-d$\n3. $b = e$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a83c00b2-50f6-5c7b-8840-b985fe5debb0",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "bd488342-3a67-56a6-87e4-42d8cb8b74ac",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "b4bcfde0-3842-57d2-8122-90bb6dac8e9e",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "III only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "ea2564b6-62af-5501-a75f-9d7e0cf22de3",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "II and III only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "29069bd7-fe6b-511b-bfe9-564fdc7e75a5",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I and III only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "000152ac-d960-50c6-bf23-7b7ef806aed8",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I and II only"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "b4bcfde0-3842-57d2-8122-90bb6dac8e9e"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is false. The vectors $b$ and $e$ have the same direction. So, $b\\neq-e$.\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $c$ and $d$ have the same direction. So, $c\\neq-d$.\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, vectors $e$ and $b$ are parallel and have the same direction. Also, the magnitude of $b$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $e$. So, $b=e$.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."
    },
