  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186096700,
      "id": "dc5bab6c-1ce7-58b5-a59d-cff2ce35ecca",
      "title": "Identifying Parallel Vectors From a Diagram"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7b56560d-9806-5e88-accd-81673cfdf178",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186096700/plots/46561271e0271a06bca958221ddd1f6539e01b1f9f18c7e8a2cca5d51459e5e2.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $a =-c$\n2. $c =-\\frac{3}{2}a$\n3. $b = d$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "45e35ccf-f587-54e4-bb6e-43b153b37cc3",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "cc51fdf2-0d6a-53a1-84e0-510ece306f5d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I and III only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "2a509c95-0079-50b1-bb10-20f7c98169d1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "d4c6d2b6-f774-58bc-af02-117eadada4e3",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "II and III only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "acc47039-5ef2-5302-8cd5-346250ec5914",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "II only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "a5254332-aba9-5434-9d16-9b41a12c9c04",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "III only"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "a5254332-aba9-5434-9d16-9b41a12c9c04"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is false. The magnitude of $a$ is $\\frac{2}{3}$ times the magnitude of $c$. So, $a\\neq-c$.\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $c$ and $a$ have the same direction. So, $c\\neq-\\frac{3}{2}a$.\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, vectors $d$ and $b$ are parallel and have the same direction. Also, the magnitude of $b$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $d$. So, $b=d$.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."
    },
